# CQ-15 · trait-incomplete
#
# Question: Which entities omit one of the three trait axes, and which axis is
#           missing?
# Persona:  P1 — generation-pipeline engineer. A consumer that switches on
#           countability needs to know which entities will not answer.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §5.4 (the trait bundle); §2.1 (what is unexamined)
# Form:     SELECT — one row per entity per missing axis
# Note:     This is not a conformance question. §2.1 lists Entity trait
#           completeness among the things no shape enforces in v1.x, so every
#           row below is a **conformant** document, and §8.2 is why it stays
#           that way inside v1.x. The answer is non-empty: the hand-authored
#           canonical scene omits `vso:countability` on two entities. That is
#           the finding, recorded rather than repaired — the same discipline
#           §5.13.7 applies to the geometry measurement.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

SELECT ?doc ?entity ?axis
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?doc {
    ?entity a ?kind .
    VALUES ?kind { vso:PhysicalObject vso:Aggregate vso:Substance }
    VALUES ?axis { vso:individuation vso:animacy vso:countability }
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?entity ?axis ?value }
  }
}
ORDER BY ?doc ?entity ?axis
